Source: dtbocfg
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Tim 'mithro' Ansell <me@mith.ro>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-sequence-dkms
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/ikwzm/dtbocfg
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: dtbocfg-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dkms
Description: Device Tree overlay ConfigFS userspace interface (DKMS)
 Out-of-tree Linux kernel module (dtbocfg, by Ichiro Kawazome) that exposes a
 ConfigFS interface for applying and removing Device Tree overlays at runtime
 from userspace, under /sys/kernel/config/device-tree/overlays/.
 .
 It is the same interface as the never-upstreamed CONFIG_OF_CONFIGFS patch, but
 implemented as a self-contained module on top of the in-kernel, GPL-exported
 of_overlay_fdt_apply() API -- so it needs no kernel patch, only
 CONFIG_OF_OVERLAY=y in the running kernel.
 .
 Built with DKMS against the running kernel, so the modules are rebuilt
 automatically on kernel upgrades and no custom kernel is required.
